/E (A foreign study conducted by Saleem \(2020\) examined the impact of automated inventory management systems on supply chain risk management and organizational performance among manufacturing firms in Pakistan. The study focused on determining how automation technologies improve inventory monitoring, operational efficiency, and business productivity. The researchers explained that many organizations still rely on traditional inventory management methods, which often result in inaccurate inventory records, delayed transactions, product shortages, overstocking, and poor coordination between departments. These problems negatively affect supply chain performance and reduce the overall efficiency of business operations.)
