/E (The study emphasized that automated inventory management systems are important because they help organizations manage inventory more effectively through computerized processes and digital technologies. The researchers specifically examined several technologies commonly used in automated inventory systems, including Radio Frequency Identification \(RFID\), Enterprise Resource Planning \(ERP\), Electronic Data Interchange \(EDI\), and Material Requirements Planning \(MRP\). According to the study, these technologies improve the monitoring, recording, and movement of inventory within organizations while reducing manual work and operational delays..)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
