/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 359 0 R
/T (2.1.1  Another related foreign study is Design and Implementation of Computerized Stock Management Systems: A Case Study of MIDE Supermarket by Akinsanya \(2019\). The study developed a computerized stock management system to improve inventory monitoring and reduce the problems caused by manual stock recording. The researchers explained that traditional inventory methods are time-consuming and prone to errors, which may affect business performance. The proposed system provided automated inventory tracking and organized record management for supermarkets. This study is relevant to the present study because both studies focus on improving inventory monitoring through digital systems. Similar to the proposed system, the study aimed to reduce manual work and improve inventory accuracy.)
/E (2.1.1  Another related foreign study is Design and Implementation of Computerized Stock Management Systems: A Case Study of MIDE Supermarket by Akinsanya \(2019\). The study developed a computerized stock management system to improve inventory monitoring and reduce the problems caused by manual stock recording. The researchers explained that traditional inventory methods are time-consuming and prone to errors, which may affect business performance. The proposed system provided automated inventory tracking and organized record management for supermarkets. This study is relevant to the present study because both studies focus on improving inventory monitoring through digital systems. Similar to the proposed system, the study aimed to reduce manual work and improve inventory accuracy.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
750 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 359 0 R
/T (2.1.2 Another foreign study related to the present project is Design of Computerized Inventory Management Systems for Supermarkets by Abisoye, Fatoba, and Blessing \(2013\). The study developed a computerized inventory system that automated product monitoring and sales recording for supermarkets. The researchers found that the system improved efficiency, minimized stock management problems, and reduced the risks associated with manual inventory processes. This study supports the present project because it demonstrates how automated inventory systems can improve operational efficiency and record management in retail establishments. However, the present study specifically focuses on pharmacies and convenience stores and includes barcode scanning and real-time stock updates.)
/E (2.1.2 Another foreign study related to the present project is Design of Computerized Inventory Management Systems for Supermarkets by Abisoye, Fatoba, and Blessing \(2013\). The study developed a computerized inventory system that automated product monitoring and sales recording for supermarkets. The researchers found that the system improved efficiency, minimized stock management problems, and reduced the risks associated with manual inventory processes. This study supports the present project because it demonstrates how automated inventory systems can improve operational efficiency and record management in retail establishments. However, the present study specifically focuses on pharmacies and convenience stores and includes barcode scanning and real-time stock updates.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
751 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 359 0 R
/T (2.1.3 Another related foreign study is Inventory Management Automation and Performance of Supermarkets in Western Kenya by Samuel and Ondiek \(2014\). The study investigated how automation technologies affect supermarket performance and inventory management efficiency. The findings showed that automated inventory systems improved inventory control, reduced product shortages, and enhanced business operations. This is relevant to the present study because it confirms that automation can improve inventory accuracy and operational performance in retail businesses.)
/E (2.1.3 Another related foreign study is Inventory Management Automation and Performance of Supermarkets in Western Kenya by Samuel and Ondiek \(2014\). The study investigated how automation technologies affect supermarket performance and inventory management efficiency. The findings showed that automated inventory systems improved inventory control, reduced product shortages, and enhanced business operations. This is relevant to the present study because it confirms that automation can improve inventory accuracy and operational performance in retail businesses.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [2]
>>
