/T (The study revealed that implementing a computerized inventory management system improved the efficiency of pharmacy operations. Through automation, employees were able to record and monitor inventory faster and with greater accuracy compared to manual methods. The system also helped reduce human errors in recording product quantities, expiration dates, and stock availability. In addition, the researchers emphasized that computerized systems provide organized and accessible records, making it easier for businesses to track transactions and generate inventory reports whenever needed.)
