/Title (The study further highlighted the importance of employee training and development in the successful implementation of automated inventory management systems. According to the researchers, organizations that invested in employee training achieved better results because employees became more capable of using automated technologies efficiently. The study noted that some employees initially experienced difficulties adapting to automated systems due to limited technical knowledge and resistance to organizational change. However, proper training programs helped employees understand the system more effectively and increased their confidence in using digital technologies.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2027 0 R
/Next 2050 0 R
>>
endobj
2047 0 obj
<<
/Title (Sharp, Rogers, and Preece \(2019\) emphasized that user-centered design is a foundational principle in developing efficient and usable software systems. Their framework advocates for continuous user involvement throughout the design and development process to ensure that systems align with actual user needs. This principle is directly applicable to the development of a pharmacy and convenience store management system, where ease of use by non-technical staff is essential.)
/Dest [68 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2051 0 R
/Next 2028 0 R
>>
endobj
