2050 0 obj
<<
/Title (Despite the positive findings, the study identified several challenges encountered during the implementation of automated inventory systems. The transition from manual inventory management to computerized systems required financial investment, technical infrastructure, and skilled personnel. Organizations needed the support of IT professionals and technology specialists to install, configure, and maintain the systems properly. In addition, the implementation process required time and organizational adjustments because employees had to adapt to new operational procedures and digital workflows.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
